Z||000000||David Gamache||03-26-2000||07:32 PM||||I am working on an 88 fiero with a 2.5L.<BR>I heard a rattle in the exhaust,removed the cat and found the biscut shrank from excessive heat. The biscut was rattling around kike a brick in a box. One problem located. But what caused the excessive heat? <BR>I removed the o2 sensor and found it was red as the Arizona desert. I next removed the exhaust manifold and found the center ports as red as the o2 sensor. I am thinking pin hole cracks in the manifold weld allowing air into manifold or bad o2 sensor. Does any have any other thoughts? What else would cause the two center ports and not the two outer ports to get so hot? The car runs good otherwise.||||reg||1
